    <description>ALF-RS-04 FR3/FR4/FR5: Sales Rep-facing Quick Action on Appraisal. Blocks submission until at least one AppraisalItem (vehicle detail) and at least one uploaded file (360 images) exist, then reassigns the record to the AF_Q_UsedCarTeam queue (Status=Visit Scheduled) and notifies + tasks every queue member — same Get Queue / Get Queue Members / Loop / Send Notification pattern as AF_FL_Lead_QueueRouting. Owner intentionally moves to the queue (not left with the rep) so Used Car Team members gain native record access without a viewAllRecords grant; AF_InitiatingSalesRep__c preserves who to hand it back to. RS-04 fix 2026-09-09: Get_Images previously queried ContentDocumentLink filtered only on LinkedEntityId, with no file-type filter — this silently counted the auto-generated Book-In Sheet PDF (always attached via AF_FL_AppraisalItem_GenerateBookInSheet with FirstPublishLocationId=this Appraisal) as satisfying &quot;at least one image,&quot; letting a rep submit for evaluation with zero real photos. Fixed by switching to a direct ContentVersion query (FirstPublishLocationId + FileType, both native fields — no cross-object traversal), mirroring the exact pattern AF_FL_AppraisalItem_GenerateBookInSheet&apos;s Get_Existing_Sheet already proved works reliably in this org after an earlier cross-object ContentDocumentLink.ContentDocument.Title filter caused an unhandled fault on every insert. FileType is now required to be one of JPG/JPEG/PNG/HEIC/GIF, so the PDF (FileType=PDF) can no longer satisfy this gate — verified live 2026-09-09. RS-04 fix 2026-09-09 (second pass): photos moved from the Appraisal to each AppraisalItem (per-vehicle gallery, afAppraisalMediaGallery now lives on AppraisalItem_Record_Page instead of Appraisal_Record_Page) - the single Get_Images lookup checking &quot;at least one image anywhere on the Appraisal&quot; no longer reflects the real requirement for a multi-vehicle trade-in, where EVERY item needs its own photo, not just one item across the whole batch. Replaced with Loop_AppraisalItems + Get_Item_Images (per-item ContentVersion query on FirstPublishLocationId=the loop item&apos;s own Id) + Item_Has_Image decision, setting var_AnyItemMissingImage=true the moment any single item is found with zero qualifying images. Has_Item_And_Images now blocks submission if var_AnyItemMissingImage is true, so a rep can no longer submit a 2-vehicle trade-in where only one car has a photo.

2026-09-13 fix (defect RS04-09, report defect #7): Assign_Owner_To_Queue previously only set OwnerId/Status, never touching AF_ApprovalStatus__c/AF_TradeInOutcome__c - so a trade-in re-submitted after already being Approved/Accepted (e.g. because a new vehicle was added post-approval, see AF_FL_AppraisalItem_ReopenOnLateAddition) kept reading Approved/Accepted while its Status simultaneously said it was back out for evaluation, a genuinely contradictory state. The quotation flows&apos; own lookups match on exactly that Approved+Accepted combination, so a trade-in that was actually reopened could still be read as a settled deduction. Added AF_ApprovalStatus__c=Pending and AF_TradeInOutcome__c=&quot;In Progress&quot; to the same update, so re-submission now correctly clears any prior decision instead of leaving it stale until an unrelated item-level change happened to roll it back indirectly.</description>
